From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:53:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] AML: keep Dolby Vision brightness matched to each picture

Match the two Dolby Vision video layers by picture timestamp and keep
that picture's base-layer timing through decoding. Missing or mistimed
packets must not shift brightness metadata to another picture. Files with
missing or incompatible layer timestamps can fail to pair instead of
falling back to arrival order.

Recognize older Matroska files that carry Dolby Vision across two tracks
using their Blu-ray source IDs. Keep both tracks bound to each other even
when the file has additional video tracks, in either stream order. Honor
explicit Dolby Vision configuration records first.

Keep the enhancement picture and its brightness metadata before HEVC end
markers. Rewriting the metadata must not skip or repeat the following
part of the picture when the serialized size changes.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLDolbyVisionTiming.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLDolbyVisionTiming.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..43e16c4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/AMLDolbyVisionTiming.h
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+/*
+ *  Copyright (C) 2026 Team CoreELEC
+ *  SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later
+ */
+
+#pragma once
+
+#include <cmath>
+#include <optional>
+
+struct AMLDoviTiming
+{
+  double pts;
+  double dts;
+};
+
+// Both layers share the demuxer's time base. Prefer presentation timestamps;
+// decode timestamps are evidence only when a presentation timestamp is absent.
+// Missing or conflicting timestamps must never silently become arrival pairing.
+// Return the base layer's timing, regardless of which layer arrived second.
+inline std::optional<AMLDoviTiming> AMLDoviMatchTiming(
+    bool firstIsEL, AMLDoviTiming first, bool secondIsEL, AMLDoviTiming second,
+    double noPts, double tolerance)
+{
+  if (firstIsEL == secondIsEL)
+    return std::nullopt;
+  const auto valid = [noPts](double value)
+  { return value != noPts && std::isfinite(value); };
+  bool matches = false;
+  if (valid(first.pts) && valid(second.pts))
+    matches = std::abs(first.pts - second.pts) < tolerance;
+  else if (valid(first.dts) && valid(second.dts))
+    matches = std::abs(first.dts - second.dts) < tolerance;
+  if (!matches)
+    return std::nullopt;
+  return firstIsEL ? second : first;
+}
